[http://courses.rice.edu/admweb/swkscat.main?p_action=COURSE&p_crn=16915&p_term=201210|"Introductory Lojban"] is a student-run one-credit course at [http://www.rice.edu/|Rice University] in Houston, USA.

The course, started on August 23, 2011, has a length of 14 weeks, with each weekly lesson lasting 1 hour. Registration is required for full participation; however, anyone is welcome to "sit in", but should contact the course presenter, Joe Anderson, beforehand. Additionally, much of the course material will be available through this page. Each Rice-registered student will be provided with a copy of the [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/The+Complete+Lojban+Language|Lojban Reference Manual]. By the end of the course, students should know the basic structure of Lojban and be able to converse in it readily.

For more information or feedback, contact the course presenter, [mailto:jandew%2Blojban@gmail.com?subject=Lojban Course at Rice University|Joe Anderson].

!Syllabus
The syllabus is found in [https://docs.google.com/viewer?a=v&pid=explorer&chrome=true&srcid=0B9_8DsEr5osgZmQ2NDk4MmItNjE5Mi00NzEyLTk5NzAtNzliNDY3MmE1N2Ni&hl=en|this Google Doc]. Explanation of the format is given in the first lesson. It is intended to be simple yet flexible, so feedback is welcome.

